# The CCITT fixtures are compressed fax streams and raw bitmaps. Git's own
# heuristic currently calls all of them binary and a clone with
# core.autocrlf=true was checked to corrupt none of them, so this changes
# nothing today. It is here because the margin is thin: the heuristic is a
# guess about content, one stream already contains no NUL byte at all, and
# several contain 0x0A bytes inside the compressed data. Regenerate the
# fixtures and that guess can go the other way.
#
# The failure it would cause is the expensive kind — the fixtures still
# present, still the right size on disk, and the decoder failing on a Windows
# runner and nowhere else. Saying "these are bytes" costs two lines.
test/fixtures/ccitt/*.bin       binary
test/fixtures/ccitt/*.expected  binary
